{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>As an eagle stirs up his nest.</b> May it be His will that just as He intended to do at Sinai, had they not sinned with the calf, so He will do in the future. And the Blessed El accepted his prayer then, as it says: אֶשְׁרְקָה לָהֶם וַאֲקַבְּצֵם כִּי פְדִיתִים (Zechariah 10:8)." "<b>Hovering over his young.</b> As it says: הִנֵּה אֶשָּׂא אֶל גּוֹיִם יָדִי וְאֶל עַמִּים אָרִים נִסִּי וְהֵבִיאוּ בָנַיִךְ בְּחֹצֶן (Isaiah 49:22)." "<b>He spreads his wings, he takes him.</b> As it says: וְאַתֶּם תְּלֻקְּטוּ לְאַחַד אַחַד בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Isaiah 27:12)." "<b>He bears him on his pinions.</b> As it says (Isaiah 60:8): מִי אֵלֶּה כָּעָב תְּעוּפֶינָה."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Reading וְקִבֵּל as 'and He accepted'; the subject is the Blessed El."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:01.980356428Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}